### Describe the bug

When a query fails after the server has started streaming the body **and** `http_write_exception_in_output_format = 1`, ClickHouse writes the error as one more JSON row — `{"exception": "Code: 395. DB::Exception: ..."}` — and then **ends the body normally**: no `__exception__` trailer frame, no connection cut, `curl` exits 0.

`ResultSet.stream()` splits the body on newlines and hands every line to the caller as a `Row`, and the only mid-stream error check is the tagged-trailer detection (`extractErrorAtTheEndOfChunk`, gated on a `\r` before the newline). The in-band JSON error row has no `\r`, so nothing detects it. The caller gets a **truncated result set plus one extra row whose only key is `exception`, and no error at all** — the query failure is silently lost. `ResultSet.json()` on `JSONEachRow` goes through `stream()`, so it is affected identically.

This is the default server behaviour on **25.8** (`http_write_exception_in_output_format` defaults to `1` there), which is still a supported LTS, and it is reachable on any newer server whose profile/user settings or query settings turn the setting on.

Note the existing test fixture [`packages/client-common/__tests__/fixtures/stream_errors.ts:18`](https://github.com/ClickHouse/clickhouse-js/blob/main/packages/client-common/__tests__/fixtures/stream_errors.ts#L18) explicitly sets `http_write_exception_in_output_format: false`, so the current stream-error tests never exercise this path.

This is distinct from #1034 (tagged `__exception__` block lost as `Error: aborted` under compression) and from PR #803 (opt-in transformer for the 25.11+ tagged trailer) — neither touches the in-band JSON error row.

### ClickHouse server version

`26.9.19.9`, run with `http_write_exception_in_output_format = 1` per query, which reproduces the 25.8 default wire behaviour exactly. Verified with `curl` first: HTTP 200, `curl` exit code 0, body ends with the `{"exception": ...}` line, zero occurrences of `__exception__` in the body (the `X-ClickHouse-Exception-Tag` header is still sent, but no tagged frame follows).

### Steps to reproduce

Integration test (`packages/client-node/__tests__/integration/`), run with `npm --prefix packages/client-node run test:integration -- run <file>`:

```ts
