### Describe the bug

`@clickhouse/client-web` sends the HTTP request and resolves when its `abort_signal` was already aborted before the call. This affects `query`, `command`, `exec`, and `insert`. An abort that happens after dispatch still rejects normally.

Reproduced with published `@clickhouse/client-web@1.25.0` and current main (`5b7f7e46b369910fd2d008619c0a39f7028f3cf8`). The same behavior reproduces in Chromium 156 through the built public Web package; each already-aborted operation sends one real loopback HTTP request.

### Steps to reproduce

1. In an empty directory, run `npm install @clickhouse/client-web@1.25.0`.
2. Save the code below as `repro.mjs`.
3. Run `node repro.mjs` on Node.js 24.

