```
FAIL  folds a bare Enum with a big ordinal as Enum16
AssertionError: expected 1 to be 2        // only 1 of the 2 bytes consumed

FAIL  folds a bare Enum with ordinal 128 as Enum16
AssertionError: expected 1 to be 2

FAIL  does not desync the following column
AssertionError: expected [ '-24', 3 ] to deeply equal [ 'a', 7 ]
```

The small-ordinal control (`Enum('a' = 1)`) passes, so only the out-of-`Int8`-range case is wrong.

Expected: `"a"` in every case, and `["a", 7]` for the two-column stream.
Actual: 1 byte consumed instead of 2, value `"-24"`, and the next column reads the stray high byte.

## Suggested fix

In `astToReader`'s `EnumDataType` branch, when `node.name` is the bare `Enum`, derive the width from the ordinals — `Enum16` if any value is outside `-128..127`, else `Enum8` — the same rule the server applies. Explicit `Enum8` / `Enum16` keep their current behaviour. (An explicit `Enum8('a' = 1000)` is rejected by the server, so no width inference is needed there.)

