## Suggested fix

`packages/client-common/src/parse/column_types.ts:324-358` — add `case "0" -> "\0"`, `case "b" -> "\b"`, `case "f" -> "\f"` (and, for completeness with the server's `parseEscapeSequence`, `a` -> `\x07`, `v` -> `\v`, `e` -> `\x1B`) to the `switch` in `unescapeEnumName`. Note `\0` must never consume the following digits — `\012` is NUL followed by the text `12`, not an octal escape. The `@clickhouse/datatype-parser` lexer (`packages/datatype-parser/src/lexer.ts:107-136`) already implements exactly this table and can be used as the reference.

