### Root cause

- Chromium discards the received but unread body data when the response ends with a network error.
- `packages/client-web/src/result_set.ts:262` connects `response.body` to the row transform with `pipeThrough`. Its backpressure leaves the tail of the body in the browser when the reader is slow, and the exception check (`result_set.ts:197-206`) sees only the bytes that reach the transform.

The browser test `packages/client-web/__tests__/integration/web_stream_error_handling.test.ts` does not reach the in-band path on 26.9. Browsers send `Accept-Encoding: gzip, deflate, br, zstd`, so the server sends zstd. The compressed output of the test fixture before the error is small, so the server returns a normal HTTP 500.

The client cannot get back the bytes that Chromium discards. A maintainer must decide between a read-ahead buffer in `stream()` and a clearer error.

